                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Lets start with the pros:\nThe game had  a decent seletion of cars as well as buses and trucks\n........?\nEasy achievements if you are into them\n.......?\nNudity?\nThats all I can think off\n\nNow for a massive list of cons:\nAI cars drive in surges, often braking suddenly causing you to hit them.\nAI cars often drive 20-50kph below the speen limit.\nAI cars often fail to follow road rules. Running red lights, hitting pedestrians, failing to give way.\nAI cars never indicate.\nAI cars will change into your lane regardlessif you are right next to them or not\nStop signs have absolutely no meaning in this game.\nExcept on the highway map, you can drive anywhere you want on the road (or on the side) as long as you dont cross the center if it is a solid line.\nCars are oversized for the roads, Buses barely fit.\nCity corners are square which is hard to turn a car around. Buses have to drive on the sidewalk.\nPedestrian crossing are randomly placed, usually with no lighting which makes nighttime driving pretty hazardous.\nPedestrians WILL cross the road regardless if you are too close to stop. They WILL walk into the side of a bus causing a penalty.\nLights at smaller intersection change rapidly and will cause you to lose points if you have not exited in time (buses nearly always lose points).\nNo cabin view, which is ok for cars, but makes driving a bus challenging.\nTerrible mouse control for adjusting view. No options for quick change or centering. Need to fight to looking backwards.\nKeyboard driving controls are terrible making driving on the highway map near impossible.\nLow beam does nothing. High beam is nearly as good as you would expect from low beam. Limit cone width. Signs do not reflect the light until you are nearly on top of them. No penalty for driving with high beam all the time. no option to switch from high beam to low beam.\nSign visiblity is low so you barely have time to see a speed change and react.\nAny Steam notifiactions pop up right over your speed, despite 2 corners having absolutley nothing in them.\nThere is more but I think you get the general idea.\n\nFor a driving game I would rate this 2/10\nFor a driving game that claims to educate, I am hesitant to give 1/10\nBTW, I lied about the nudity so looks like that brings it to 0/10\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1416773407,
